    "title": "2026 World Baseball Classic: How to watch the Japan vs. Venezuela quarterfinal game tonight, where to stream and more",
    "text": "Japan entered the 2026 World Baseball Classic as the reigning champions, and so far they've dominated the tournament, walking away from the pool stage with an undefeated 4-0 record. (Los Angeles Dodgers star Shohei Ohtani isn't even pitching for the team during the WBC, but he has produced two grand slams that have contributed to their wins.) The team will now advance to the quarterfinals where they'll face Venezuela on Saturday night at Miami's LoanDepot Park.The Japan vs. Venezuela quarterfinal game will air on Fox and FOX Deportes tonight at 9 p.m. ET. The game will also stream on FOX One. Here's everything you need to know about how to watch the 2026 World Baseball Classic, including a complete schedule of games and where to watch them all.AdvertisementDate: Saturday, March 14Time: 9 p.m. ETChannels: Fox, Fox DeportesStreaming: FOX One, DirecTV, Fubo & moreJapan vs. Venezuela quarterfinal game time: The Japan vs. Venezuela game at the World Baseball Classic will take place Saturday, March 14, at 9 p.m. ET.Japan vs. Venezuela quarterfinal game channel:The Japan vs. Venezuela game will be broadcast live on Fox and in Spanish on FOX Deportes.Where to watch the World Baseball Classic without cableEvery single World Baseball Classic game will stream on FOX One. You can also catch games that are broadcast on Fox, FS1 and FS2 on platforms like DirecTV and Fubo.FOX One is a new streaming service from FOX that launched in 2025. With a subscription to FOX One, you can tune in to all your favorite FOX channels like FOX News, FOX Sports, FOX Weather, FS1, FS2, FOX Business, FOX Deportes, Big Ten Network (B1G), and local FOX stations all in one place, and this year, they'll be streaming every single game of the 2026 World Baseball Classic. FOX One offers live programming, as well as shows and movies on demand. The base price for FOX One will cost $19.99 a month, or you can save with an annual subscription for $199.99. World Baseball Classic PoolsPool A: Canada, Colombia, Cuba, Panama and Puerto RicoAdvertisementPool B: Brazil, Great Britain, Italy, Mexico and United StatesPool C: Australia, Chinese Taipei, Czechia, Japan and KoreaPool D: Dominican Republic, Israel, Netherlands, Nicaragua and VenezuelaWorld Baseball Classic ScheduleMarch 13QuarterfinalsSouth Korea vs. Dominican Republic, 6:30 p.m. ET, Miami (FS2, Fox Deportes)USA vs. Canada, 8 p.m. ET, Houston (FOX, Fox Deportes)March 14QuarterfinalsPuerto Rico vs. Italy, 3 p.m. ET, Houston (FS1, Fox Deportes)Venezuela vs. Japan, 9 p.m. ET, Miami (FOX, Fox Deportes)March 15SemifinalsTBD vs. TBD, 8 p.m. ET, Miami (FS1, Fox Deportes)March 16SemifinalsTBD vs. TBD, 8 p.m. ET, Miami (FS1, Fox Deportes)March 17FinalsTBD vs. TBD, 8 p.m. ET, Miami (FOX, Fox Deportes)",
